  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is establishing a reliable performance baseline for the RNA modality before exploring more complex designs. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest RNA configuration: PCA-2000 is a fast, well-understood linear encoder, and singleprofile avoids confounding from aggregation choices. This experiment isolates the raw signal strength of the RNA modality under minimal modeling assumptions. It serves as a reference floor: if RNA alone performs well, subsequent experiments can test whether multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), or multimodal fusion add value; if it performs poorly, I can pivot toward image-only or multimodal configurations. Choosing the simplest valid baseline first avoids overcommitting to a complex architecture before knowing whether the underlying signal is informative, and it maximizes the interpretability of all 9 remaining experiments by giving a clean anchor point for comparison."
}

